WEBVTT

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.295
AG: Wait a minute.
So you killed happy hour?

00:08:32.319 --> 00:08:35.626
VM: We didn't hear a single complaint,
to be honest with you. (Laughs)

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.051
AG: You didn't have group of party
animals working with you, apparently.

00:08:39.075 --> 00:08:40.431
VM: What was interesting is,

00:08:40.455 --> 00:08:42.915
I think part of the reason
we didn't hear complaints

00:08:42.939 --> 00:08:46.329
is because we had created other spaces
and opportunities during the day

00:08:46.353 --> 00:08:48.476
for people to spend time together.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.409
AG: If you've ever been to a happy hour
that was more about drinking than bonding,

00:08:52.433 --> 00:08:53.866
this might sound familiar.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.343
Research suggests that company parties
rarely build new bridges.

00:08:57.367 --> 00:09:00.131
People gravitate toward
their existing friends and groups,